    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1059">

                <pb facs="0786" n="670" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg670"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.11/3699.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul Lespinasse to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Froutera</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-04-20">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 20, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your April 20, was received this evening. I am now advising Americans in this
                    State and northern Chiapas by telegraph to withdraw. Will report fully
                    to-morrow. Must I provide passage for destitute Americans as on the first
                    occasion? It would be advisable to allow Americans to enter New Orleans and
                    Galveston.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lespinasse</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
